# Flutter / Dart
- Preserve existing architecture, state management, dependency injection, navigation and folder conventions.
- Keep null safety intact; avoid unnecessary null assertions and dynamic typing.
- Dispose owned controllers, focus nodes, animations, streams and subscriptions.
- Across async gaps, verify lifecycle safety before using BuildContext/widget state; use mounted checks when required.
- Avoid blocking the UI isolate with heavy CPU/synchronous I/O.
- Prefer const/immutability where appropriate without unrelated churn.
- Keep business logic out of presentation widgets when service/domain/state layers exist.
- Handle relevant loading, empty, error, offline, retry and cancellation states.
- Preserve localization and RTL/LTR behavior.
- Do not hand-edit generated registrants/serialization/localization files; modify their source and regenerate.
- Verify package compatibility from actual pubspec/lockfile before adding dependencies.
- Run configured static analysis, targeted tests, and relevant build verification when compilation/platform integration can be affected.
